// Edexcel GCSE (9–1) Mathematics 1MA1 — Algebra, batch 1.
// Specification references (Issue 2, June 2015; Foundation and Higher lists compared 22 October 2026):
//   A1 notation · A2 substitution, including scientific formulae · A3 vocabulary: expressions,
//   equations, formulae, identities, inequalities, terms, factors · A4 simplify and manipulate:
//   collect like terms, single brackets, common factors, two binomials (Higher: two or more),
//   x² + bx + c including difference of two squares (Higher: ax² + bx + c), laws of indices ·
//   A5 use and rearrange formulae · A6 equation vs identity (show-that arguments not marked) ·
//   A17 solve linear equations algebraically · A21 (part) form and solve equations.
// Not in this batch: algebraic fractions (A4 Higher), A6 proof, A7 functions, A17 graphical solutions.
// All teaching text and questions are original.
